//! Strata consensus engine — GENERATED by `ggen sync run` from the
//! `strata-consensus-pack` ontology (st:CONSENSUS_CONSTANTS + the
//! st:ForkChoice / st:AdversarialCase law). Hand-quality module:
//! self-contained, no external crates, so `rustc --test` works directly.
//! Do not edit by hand; regenerate rather than patching.
//!
//! Roadmap slice S8: docs/sjira/v26.10.8/STRATA-BLOCKCHAIN-ROADMAP.md
//!
//! Law provenance: S8 GREENFIELD (roadmap S5/S8 precondition outcome — no
//  nonce, difficulty, or fork-choice code exists anywhere to reuse; the
//! BUSL-1.1 unibit tree is off-limits and its "TruthBlock" is a memory
//! region, not a blockchain block). Fork choice is formalized CONCEPTUALLY
//! as the PN64-style transition lattice: each mined block is a transition,
//! chain work accumulates over the lattice, and the selected tip is the
//! lattice maximum under heaviest-work with the deterministic lower-nonce
//! tie-break.
//!
//! Pattern provenance (comments only, no cross-pack imports — FM-PACK-018):
//! - strata-chain-pack (S5): the Block shape, header encoding, PoW digest
//!   law SHA-256(header || nonce u64 BE), leading-zero-bit difficulty
//!   metric, and the validate law shape (height/parent-hash/PoW) are
//!   provenance-copied PATTERN from packs/strata-chain-pack
//!   generated/chain_engine.rs.
//! - strata-hash-pack (S1): the SHA-256 implementation follows the
//!   zero-crate FIPS 180-4 pattern of packs/strata-hash-pack
//!   generated/hash_merkle.rs (same K-table / H0, correctness pinned by
//!   the published FIPS vectors in tests).
//! - strata-net-pack (S7): eclipse/spam guarding pre-commits the S9
//!   hardening bar over gossip-shaped peer tables and slot counters.

